# Copy to .env and adjust for a non-default backend location.
#
# Left unset, the app calls relative /api/v1/... paths. In dev, vite.config.ts proxies /api to
# http://localhost:8000 (override with VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET, a dev-only shell env var, not this
# file — Vite never exposes it to client code). In production, relative paths mean the frontend
# must be served from the same origin as the API (e.g. behind one reverse proxy); if it isn't,
# set VITE_API_BASE_URL to the API's full origin and make sure that origin's ALLOWED_ORIGINS
# (backend .env) includes wherever this app is served from.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
